.th LIST I ?/?/76
.sh NAME
list \*- ascii source lister
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd list
[ \fB-\fRoptions ] file [ [ \fB-\fRoptions ] [ file ] ] ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
List produces a printed listing of one or more files on standard output.
The output is separated into pages headed by the file name,
page number, and the creation date of the file.
.s3
List examines each character of the input file
and prints the 96 ASCII graphics; the ASCII TAB ('\\t')
and NEWLINE ('\\n') characters are the only control characters
which "list" recognizes.
Lines which are longer than the
specified paper width are truncated and a
DEL printed as the
last character.
If you wish lines to be "folded", use the
"f" parameter.
List works as a filter if no input file name is given.
.s3
Options (preceded by a `-') apply to all following files
unless reset between files.
.s3
.ft I
.lp +9 8
option	meaning
.ft R
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBc\fR	format output for CRT presentation.
Release each page by typing a return.
Sets "\fB-m\fR0\fBl\fR20".
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBt\fIn\fR	set tab spacing to \fIn\fR (default 8).
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBl\fIn\fR	set page length to \fIn\fR lines (default 58 + 2 header lines).
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBn\fR	do not print line numbers.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBw\fIn\fR	set paper width to \fIn\fR columns (default
80).
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBm\fIn\fR	set left margin width to \fIn\fR columns
(default 0)
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB+\fIn\fR	begin printing at page \fIn\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fB:\fIn\fR	stop printing after page \fIn\fR.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBp\fR	direct output directly to printer ("/dev/lp").
The spooler \fIlpr\fR (I) should be used for all but very large
listings.
.s3
.lp +9 8
\fBf\fR	fold output (default mode is truncate).
.i0
.dt
.s3
To print a file on a CRT terminal with a line
width of 60, the following command is appropriate:

	list -cw60 filename
	RETURN	<----- (to release pages)

.sh "SEE ALSO"
cat(I), cp(I), pr(I)
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
none; files not found are ignored
.sh AUTHOR
(\ deservedly unknown\ )
.sh BUGS
This atrocious program is quite useable
provided care is taken with the options:
.lp +9 8
1.	They are order dependant:- l after c, n after w, m after c;
.lp +9 8
2.	w and (m or n) are mutually dependant - so don't use them together!
